<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Imbabura Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Imbabura is a province in the northern highlands of Ecuador, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibarra">Ibarra</a>, named after the Imbabura volcano. It was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the Caranqui, who resisted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> in the late 15th century. Today it is known for the indigenous market town of Otavalo and its mountain lakes, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yahuarcocha">Yahuarcocha</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/imbabura-province.jpg" alt="Imbabura Province" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Imbabura_des_del_sud.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
